AR FEATURES  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma is essentially negative for E cadherin  The in situ carcinoma shows areas with ductal differentiation and other areas with a lobular like growth pattern  However  it is not clear that the two processes are distinct in situ lesions  Indeed  a morphologic spectrum between the two exists  favoring that they represent a related neoplastic process  Results of E cadherin stains in the in situ component are variable  there is strong positivity in some areas with ductal differentiation  only focal and very weak positivity in other areas with ductal differentiation  and negativity in areas with a lobular like growth pattern  Given the overall morphologic features and the fact that ductal carcinomas may lose E cadherin expression  these changes may simply represent biologic variability of a fundamentally ductal type neoplasm  However  to acknowledge the lobular like pattern of spread and minimal to absent E cadherin reactivity in some areas  both the invasive carcinoma and some of the in situ carcinoma are classified as having both ductal and lobular features  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   2 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm with a 0 12cm satellite nodule  based on combined gross and microscopic measurements   GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 to 3  MARGIN OF CARCINOMA IN SITU  Carcinoma in situ focally extends to  0 1cm from the posterior margin  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  2  SMALL FOCI OF EARLY FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies tha